  "body": "### Summary\nTwo-line summary: the 2026-11-10 capture wave (#737-#766) merged ten capture PRs one after another, and every merge left a conflict, a stale branch or a manual step behind. This issue lists that clean-up and the tooling that stops the next wave from needing it.\n\n### Scope (one checkbox each; split into its own PR as needed)\n\n**1. MANIFEST ↔ corpus consistency check** (`area: tooling`, cloud)\n- A re-check on #758/#764 reported a duplicate \"Store\" id and 13 corpus ids without a MANIFEST row (`T11`, `T11h`, `T14`, `T14h`, `T20`-`T24`, `T30`-`T33`). On inspection these are **false positives**:\n  - \"Store\" is the header of the two legacy-store tables;\n  - the T ids sit in grouped rows (`| T11, T11h |`, `| T20, T21, T24 |`, `| T30, T31 |`) or in prose.\n- No real gap found today. The gap is that **nothing checks it**.\n- [ ] Add a check, in `tooling/fixtures` or the Docs consistency job: every `corpus.json` id is named in a MANIFEST row, grouped ids included; every MANIFEST capture id exists in the corpus; table headers are ignored. Tests first.\n- [ ] Optionally split grouped rows, or tolerate them explicitly in the check.\n\n**2. `corpus.json` serial conflicts** (`area: tooling`, cloud)\n- Each capture PR appends its rows at the end of `tooling/fixtures/corpus.json`, so every merge conflicted with the next PR. Seven PRs on 2026-11-10 each needed a merge of dev-swift, a scripted union and a re-check, and each cost a macOS CI run.\n- [ ] Remove the conflict class, as #612/#620 did for the ledger: either one file per capture batch (`tooling/fixtures/corpus.d/<batch>.json`, read by `anonymize.py`), or rows sorted by id. Keep `check --corpus` the arbiter, and migrate the existing file in one PR.\n\n**3. Merged branches left on the remote** (maintainer)\n- 99 head branches of merged PRs are still on `ezzz/HFRnow` (count of 2026-11-10 22:00 UTC). Cloud sessions cannot delete branches: the proxy refuses it.\n- [ ] Maintainer: delete them, or turn on \"Automatically delete head branches\" through `scripts/configure-repo.sh` (a repository setting, operator's call). Branches `legacy/*` and `master` are out of scope.\n\n**4. Mac clean-up after the merges** (`host: mac`)\n- [ ] The items of the \"Mac report m4-captures\" on #368 (local branches, worktrees, raw captures kept outside the repository), once posted there.\n\n**5. Orchestration notes** (`area: docs`)\n- [ ] `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`: a cloud orchestrator's background scripts do not survive the container's idle restarts (three losses on 2026-11-10). After an APPROVE, use GitHub auto-merge (`squash`); the merger still closes the issue on its next pass (§8). Chain capture PRs by hand.\n- [ ] Add the macOS tempo rule (operator, 2026-11-10, #368: at most 2 active macOS jobs by day, 5 by night, before a push or a ready) and the child-archiving rule to the same file.\n- [ ] LESSONS entry: a script that updates a branch from a second worktree moves the branch under a checkout that has it checked out; keep the main checkout detached.\n\n### Sources\n- #368 (state comment and operating rules of 2026-11-10); re-check verdicts on #758 and #764; the merge commits on #737, #741, #748, #738, #758 and #764.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Items 1, 2 and 5 merged, with tests for 1 and 2.\n- [ ] Items 3 and 4 done by the maintainer, or explicitly declined, on this issue.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
